WEBVTT

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:27.290
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.680
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:44.940
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.240
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:01.540
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.800
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.470
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:28.020
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.200
Well, well. There were a few of 
those toys left lying around.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.370
Their joining the fight 
will make no difference.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.830
Hey, Zefiris. We'll follow your lead.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.620
Is that you, Senes?

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.900
What are those?

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.290
Emulating Dragoon System...

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.750
Gigases.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.710
Here they come.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.810
"The Passion of the Lonely God"

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:14.520
Chris!

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.150
This way.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.330
Chris, where are we going?

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.870
Do you have some objective in mind?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.420
Chris?

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.330
We're going to the castle.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.790
The castle?

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.400
Let's go.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.680
Come down from the sky, 
thou moon-devouring wolf,

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.390
and let thy rage take 
the form of destruction!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.970
Raquel!

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.520
Stay close to me!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.950
Those Bugs are awfully impressive.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.980
Aren't they, though?

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.370
Actually, that was the first 
time I ever tried that.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.950
Someone! Is someone here?!

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.120
Anyone! Protect me!

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.350
Quickly appease the wrath of God!

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.590
Why won't this thing open?!

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.770
Shannon...

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.570
What in the world are those things?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.370
Surely a wise man like Your 
Highness already knows the answer.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.370
Cardinal Hogue...

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.410
Within those lights are the absolute beings

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.580
whom the Church of Mauser calls 
angels, the messengers of God.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.440
There is no longer any point 
in hiding it from you.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:05.010
For they have appeared 
openly before humanity.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.680
Those are... the messengers of God?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.980
If only we ourselves had killed 
the Scrapped Princess sooner...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.480
What do you mean by that?

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:21.400
I mean that if it were not for Your 
Highness' sister, the Scrapped Princess,

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.910
this tragedy would not have happened.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.600
Sutton.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.390
Climb! Go higher!

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.600
Circle higher! Don't let 
them fire towards the city!

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.490
Shut up! I know that!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.480
Drake!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.110
My repair systems can handle it!

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.570
Do you think you can destroy 
us with the likes of those?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.070
Don't make me laugh.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.490
Don't underestimate us, monster.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:17.830
This way!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.590
Climb! Climb!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.840
I know, I know!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.690
Are those Dragoons, too?

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.690
Those were produced late in the war.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.020
Unlike the ARFFI series, they aren't 
equipped with a virtual personality.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.370
These were buried in Giat.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.780
We tinkered with them with Natalie.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.160
Tell us, Chris, what are you 
planning to do at the castle?

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.160
What will you do once you 
see the Scrapped Princess?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.080
I won't force you along.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.700
If you have doubts about my actions,

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.090
you don't have to come.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.510
Hey, Shannon Cassul.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.930
Leave that red one to me.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.970
All right.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.690
General...

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.710
General Peters-Stahl!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.290
What is it?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.140
What are your orders, sir?

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.840
In the event of the king's incapacitation,

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.320
command authority is transferred to you, sir.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.920
It looks like we picked the 
wrong people to negotiate with.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.190
Mauser wants this matter brought to an end.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.890
Execute the Scrapped Princess!

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:56.850
We'll present her head to God's messengers!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.280
Please, stop this... Stop, already!

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.520
Why are you doing this for me?

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.200
What's going on?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.170
You're...

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.580
Hold still.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.870
We'll talk later.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.050
Pacifica Cassul, you're coming with us.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.390
Huh? What's going on?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.230
Let's go.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.410
Say, Chris, I know it's a little 
late to be bringing this up,

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.620
but we're in clear violation of orders here.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.040
Start explaining.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.620
What do you think you're doing, 
breaking her out like this?

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.810
The Baroness told me something.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.590
She said to never let go of my own free will.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.530
I was involved in two attempts 
on this girl's life,

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:17.180
and then I looked into the Grendel 
Revelations on the Baroness' orders.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.560
Is this girl really the poison 
that will destroy the world?

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.520
You all saw those monsters, didn't you?

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.080
Are those things really God's messengers?

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.810
As for me, I'm staying with her.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:34.950
What about the rest of you?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.970
You're asking that now?

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.910
Don't be silly. Do you even need to ask?

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.250
Uh, what if one of us said no?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.750
Are you saying no?

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.290
It doesn't matter to me.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.090
Then pipe down.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.920
Read the writing on the wall.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:51.800
Let's go.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.130
Get up.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.120
Where do you think you're going?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.490
I don't recall there being any orders 
to move the Scrapped Princess.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.700
The Baroness' orders?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:20.560
No, sir.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.130
We're acting on our own initiative,

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.590
not anyone's orders.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.350
I see.

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.900
Suit yourselves.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.010
Orders have come down to 
kill the Scrapped Princess,

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.170
but no one said anything about 
not letting her get away.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.650
Colonel...

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.660
But I assume that you <i>do </i>realize what 
position this will put you in, right?

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.140
Yes, sir.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:46.600
You're sure about this?

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:50.560
C'mon.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.230
Are you all right, Shannon?

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.610
It's nothing.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.110
If we keep wasting time up 
here, Pacifica's going to be...

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.580
Um...

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.740
Where are you taking me?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.130
Don't worry, you can trust us.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.880
People who say, "You can trust us"...

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:03.000
Those are the people that 
I can't seem to trust.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.690
Most people don't go out of 
their way to be nice to me.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.850
I'm taking you to your brother and sister.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.580
So could you please be quiet for a while?

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:16.130
But... Why are you doing this?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.860
I'm not really sure.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:19.790
I guess it's because...

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.820
In the end, I did it because I wanted to.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:28.820
This is probably the first time I've 
ever done something because I wanted to

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:32.790
since I was raised to be 
a Special Forces soldier.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:38.420
But for me, the thought of 
being someone's friend...

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.510
Of wanting to help them...

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.630
Being able to think that way on my own...

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:46.260
It makes me... How can I put it?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.810
It makes me really happy.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.730
Does that answer your question?

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.690
Thank you.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:29.470
Senes!

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.690
They were awfully gung-ho 
when they showed up,

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.440
but they sure didn't put up much of a fight.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.820
It's not too late. We're 
still willing to spare you.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:44.130
Surrender, and forget about 
everything that's happened.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.450
Turn a blind eye to your sister,

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:52.500
and we'll leave you and your friends 
alive after we've carried out the reset.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.330
Give it a rest.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.670
"Messengers of God," my ass. 
You're just overblown puppets.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.540
You bastards aren't absolute.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.250
Or even righteous.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:04.800
You seriously expect me to believe 
a word you say after all this?!

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.300
What foolishness.

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:16.220
Why do you humans go to such lengths 
in the hopes of defying fate?

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.190
Is it out of devotion 
to simpleminded heroism?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:26.030
Is your sister worth risking 
the world's future for?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.040
You seem to think so,

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:31.410
but haven't you only been made to think that?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.660
I agonized over it. I had my doubts.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.370
There were lots of times 
when I wanted to give up.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:41.280
But I was overlooking one important thing.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.170
Oh? And what's that?

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:49.180
Who said that I had to choose 
protecting Pacifica <i>or </i>the world?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.240
You expect me to choose one over the other?!

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:56.050
Call it what you will... 
Idealism or whatever...

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:59.190
But I'm gonna do everything 
I can to have it both ways!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.150
So be it.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:04.610
Then die as you stay true to your ideals.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:13.540
Forgive me.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.160
This is bad, Shannon...

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.390
I can't take much more...

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.560
Shall I finish him off?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.350
Suit yourself.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.830
You okay?

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.080
Thanks...

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.290
Drake, Ruth, keep it up!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.580
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.050
We're withdrawing. Steyr is dead.

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.900
Abort the reset operation, too.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:07.370
We need to regroup.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.880
Understood.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.990
The bastards ran away...

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.920
What happened to the red one?

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.050
She was completely destroyed.

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:21.980
We've done enough. Let's go back, Zefiris.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:35.490
They're dissolving?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.330
Raquel! To the castle!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.960
Yes, let's go.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.370
Miss Raquel, I take it?

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.280
Pacifica!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.530
Winia? Leo?

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.750
What are you doing here?

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:53.870
Dragunov! What are you doing here, girl?

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.780
How'd you get here?!

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.740
Look, Raquel! It's Dragunov!

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.160
Miss Pacifica...

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.810
Thank goodness...

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.420
Thank goodness she's all right.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.410
It must have been rough.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.460
Was it hard for you?

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.710
Yeah...

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.080
It was frustrating.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.670
It was really frustrating, somehow.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.410
Lots of people died, didn't they?

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.400
That's what I hear.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.640
I... If I wasn't...

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.220
If it weren't for me, they'd still...

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.380
Pacifica.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.610
I know...

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:14.980
I know.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:19.440
But I keep thinking it.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.640
I can't stop myself from thinking it.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.560
If I died right here, it would...

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:33.550
Shannon?

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.330
Do you want to die?

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.490
Do you want to die and get it all over with?

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:57.340
This sword of mine is here to protect 
your life or take it, whichever you want.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:02.790
If you want to die, I'll 
kill you where you stand.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.860
No matter what you choose,

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:09.210
it won't change the fact 
that someone will die.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.890
I don't care what people call you.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:17.460
I don't care what everyone 
in the world says about you.

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.920
I don't care about them.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.970
They never take responsibility 
for anyone else.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.000
They just say whatever's appropriate.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.870
Without a shred of conviction.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:34.030
So I don't give a damn about what 
those people say... not anymore.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:42.660
But if you yourself believe that you're 
the poison that will destroy the world...

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:46.130
If you wish you could disappear,

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.470
or if you want to die,

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:52.330
then there's nothing I can do to stop you.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:59.610
Because the only person who has the right 
to decide who or what you are is you.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.550
Big brother...

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:05.300
What do you want to do?

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:11.390
But... But so many people 
are dead because of me.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.270
I'm not asking about anybody else!

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.730
I'm asking you what <i>you </i>want!

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:19.440
If you want to die,

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.460
I'll kill you so quickly 
you won't feel a thing.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.730
But if you want to live,

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.740
I'll do whatever it takes to protect you.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.160
Make your decision.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.340
I...

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.090
I want to live.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.120
I want to go on living.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.620
I don't want to die.

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:47.570
I want to be with my brother, 
my sister, and my friends.

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:58.440
Then let's live. With everything we've got.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:35.950
Pacifica and the others have fled 
to the outskirts of the holy city

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:37.830
and are worried because they don't know 
when the Royal Forces will attack.

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:39.920
But if you keep wearing your clothes 
without washing them, they start to smell.

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:41.940
And it's bad for your health 
if you don't eat properly.

00:22:41.940 --> 00:22:44.000
Pacifica puts her cooking skills 
